      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1906 the Galveston, Harrisburg and San Antonio Railroad laid tracks just north of the lake, linking Smiley to regional markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://smiley.texas.gov/history",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Between 1880 and 1906 Smiley boasted a saddle factory, wire‑fence plant, chair factory, blacksmith shop, newspaper, drug store, general stores, school, Baptist church, and an I.0.0.F Lodge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://smiley.texas.gov/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1940 the community supported twelve businesses, two factories, two churches, and an estimated 500 residents.",
